Feature: Databricks PySpark script to transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 bucket to Purgo S3 folder

  The script transfers files from the Vendor S3 bucket to the Purgo S3 folder based on configuration in purgo_playground.ingest_config_master.
  Only files with active_flag = "A" are eligible. Files already present in either the Purgo S3 folder or the Archive S3 folder are excluded.
  S3 paths are dynamically retrieved from the configuration table. AWS credentials are securely accessed from Databricks secrets.

  Background:
    Given the Databricks Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the configuration table is "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And AWS credentials are retrieved from Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" with keys "access_key" and "secret_key"
    And the script retrieves s3_vendor_path, s3_landing_path, and s3_archive_path from "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And file eligibility is determined by active_flag = "A" in "purgo_playground.ingest_config_master"
    And file name matching is case-sensitive and includes file extensions
    And only top-level files are considered (no recursive subfolder processing)
    And files are copied (not moved) from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3
    And if a file with the same name exists in Purgo S3, it is skipped (not overwritten)
    And the script logs all file transfer attempts and results to "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" with file_status and file_processed_date

  Scenario: Transfer eligible files from Vendor S3 to Purgo S3 (happy path)
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 123       | data1.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data1.csv   |
      | data2.csv   |
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data2.csv   |
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveA/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      |             |
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "data1.csv" is copied from "s3://vendor-bucket/folderA/" to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingA/"
    And the file "data2.csv" is not copied because it already exists in the Purgo S3 folder
    And the file "data1.csv" is not present in the Archive S3 folder
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data1.csv" with file_status = "SUCCESS"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data2.csv" with file_status = "SKIPPED_EXISTS"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if active_flag is not "A"
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 124       | data3.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveB/    | I           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderB/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data3.csv   |
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "data3.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingB/"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data3.csv" with file_status = "SKIPPED_INACTIVE"

  Scenario: Do not transfer files if already present in Archive S3 folder
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 125       | data4.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveC/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderC/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data4.csv   |
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveC/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data4.csv   |
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "data4.csv" is not copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingC/"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data4.csv" with file_status = "SKIPPED_ARCHIVED"

  Scenario: Error when required S3 path is missing in configuration
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path | s3_landing_path | s3_archive_path | active_flag |
      | 126       | data5.csv      |                | s3://purgo-bucket/landingD/ | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveD/ | A |
    When the script is executed
    Then the script raises an error with message "Missing required S3 path in configuration for config_id 126"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data5.csv" with file_status = "ERROR_CONFIG"

  Scenario: Error when AWS credentials are missing or invalid
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script raises an error with message "AWS credentials not found in Databricks secret scope 'aws_keys'"
    And no files are transferred
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains no new records

  Scenario: File name matching is case-sensitive and includes extension
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 127       | Data6.CSV      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderE/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingE/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveE/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderE/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | data6.csv   |
      | Data6.CSV   |
    And the Purgo S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/landingE/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      |             |
    And the Archive S3 folder "s3://purgo-bucket/archiveE/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      |             |
    When the script is executed
    Then only the file "Data6.CSV" is copied to "s3://purgo-bucket/landingE/"
    And the file "data6.csv" is not copied
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "Data6.CSV" with file_status = "SUCCESS"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "data6.csv" with file_status = "SKIPPED_NOT_CONFIGURED"

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test for multiple eligible and ineligible files
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | <config_id> | <file_name>  | <s3_vendor_path>              | <s3_landing_path>              | <s3_archive_path>              | <active_flag> |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "<s3_vendor_path>" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | <vendor_file> |
    And the Purgo S3 folder "<s3_landing_path>" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | <purgo_file> |
    And the Archive S3 folder "<s3_archive_path>" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | <archive_file> |
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "<vendor_file>" is <expected_action> in "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "<vendor_file>" with file_status = "<expected_status>"

    Examples:
      | config_id | file_name    | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag | vendor_file | purgo_file | archive_file | expected_action | expected_status         |
      | 201       | fileA.csv    | s3://vendor-bucket/folderF/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingF/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveF/    | A           | fileA.csv   |            |             | copied         | SUCCESS                |
      | 202       | fileB.csv    | s3://vendor-bucket/folderG/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingG/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveG/    | A           | fileB.csv   | fileB.csv  |             | not copied     | SKIPPED_EXISTS          |
      | 203       | fileC.csv    | s3://vendor-bucket/folderH/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingH/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveH/    | A           | fileC.csv   |            | fileC.csv   | not copied     | SKIPPED_ARCHIVED        |
      | 204       | fileD.csv    | s3://vendor-bucket/folderI/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingI/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveI/    | I           | fileD.csv   |            |             | not copied     | SKIPPED_INACTIVE        |
      | 205       | fileE.csv    | s3://vendor-bucket/folderJ/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingJ/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveJ/    | A           | fileF.csv   |            |             | not copied     | SKIPPED_NOT_CONFIGURED  |

  Scenario: Log all file transfer attempts and results
    Given the script processes files "file1.csv", "file2.csv", and "file3.csv"
    When "file1.csv" is successfully copied, "file2.csv" is skipped due to existence, and "file3.csv" is skipped due to inactive config
    Then the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains
      | file_name   | file_status        |
      | file1.csv   | SUCCESS           |
      | file2.csv   | SKIPPED_EXISTS    |
      | file3.csv   | SKIPPED_INACTIVE  |

  Scenario: Do not process files in subfolders (no recursion)
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 301       | fileG.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderK/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingK/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveK/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderK/" contains files
      | file_name         |
      | fileG.csv         |
      | subfolder/fileH.csv |
    When the script is executed
    Then only the file "fileG.csv" is considered for transfer
    And the file "subfolder/fileH.csv" is not processed
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "fileG.csv"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table does not contain a record for "subfolder/fileH.csv"

  Scenario: Error when file transfer fails due to S3 permissions
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 401       | fileI.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingL/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveL/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | fileI.csv   |
    And the script does not have permission to read from "s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/"
    When the script is executed
    Then the script raises an error with message "S3 access denied for s3://vendor-bucket/folderL/"
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "fileI.csv" with file_status = "ERROR_S3_ACCESS"

  Scenario: No eligible files to transfer
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 501       | fileJ.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderM/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingM/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveM/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderM/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      |             |
    When the script is executed
    Then no files are transferred
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains no new records

  Scenario: File is not transferred if not listed in configuration
    Given the configuration table contains a record with
      | config_id | file_name      | s3_vendor_path                | s3_landing_path                | s3_archive_path                | active_flag |
      | 601       | fileK.csv      | s3://vendor-bucket/folderN/   | s3://purgo-bucket/landingN/    | s3://purgo-bucket/archiveN/    | A           |
    And the Vendor S3 folder "s3://vendor-bucket/folderN/" contains files
      | file_name   |
      | fileL.csv   |
    When the script is executed
    Then the file "fileL.csv" is not transferred
    And the "purgo_playground.s3_file_process_log" table contains a record for "fileL.csv" with file_status = "SKIPPED_NOT_CONFIGURED"
